 "relevance_note": "In a 1000-patient genomic cohort, the supplementary excerpt gives one case row with individual-level detail for a TNFAIP3 variant (\"TNFAIP3 (NM_001270508.1): c.1939A&gt;C; p.(Thr647Pro)\", tested by \"Indication based Exome\", ACMG \"PS3, PP3, PP4\"); the main text never mentions TNFAIP3.",
 "method_note": "Read the full paper by hand; the JSON was assembled by a short script that only wrote values I chose. The main text, tables and figures never mention TNFAIP3, A20 or HA20. The only TNFAIP3 content is the supplementary excerpt of Additional file 1 (13073_2023_1157_MOESM1_ESM.docx), which shows two fragments without table titles or column headers: (a) a 3-cell row 'TNFAIP3 | Autoinflammatory syndrome, familial, Behcet-like | 1' (by its shape probably the disorder-frequency table the text cites as Table S5, but the excerpt does not name it); (b) a variant row 'AD (colspan 2) | Indication based Exome | TNFAIP3 (NM_001270508.1): c.1939A&gt;C; p.(Thr647Pro) | PS3, PP3, PP4 | 6:138201240 | Novel', cut off before and after, so the case number, sex, age, phenotype and classification columns are not visible. One in-scope person was recorded from row (b). Because the paper's own case label and the table number/row position are not visible in the excerpt, the label is 'unnamed person 1' (label rule 6). The disease label was attributed to this person by linking fragment (a) (the only TNFAIP3 disorder, count 1) to fragment (b) (the only TNFAIP3 variant row); this cross-fragment link is an inference. n_patients_reported left null: the '1' in fragment (a) has no visible column header, and the text gives no TNFAIP3 patient count. is_proband = true from 'Of the 1000 probands', which covers every cohort patient. 'AD' in row (b) appears to be the disease mode of inheritance; it was not used for zygosity or inheritance (rule 8). 'Novel' in row (b) is novelty status, not a pathogenicity class, so pathogenicity is 'not reported'. PS3 is printed as an ACMG code but no functional assay is described, so functional_evidence_statement is 'not reported'. The genomic position '6:138201240' is recorded as printed; its column header and genome build are not shown. Variant values decode the HTML entity '&gt;' to '>' (spans keep '&gt;' verbatim). No phenotypic features are reported for this person, so phenotypic_features is empty and all 20 checklist items are 'not reported'. No contradictions found.",
